{%- comment -%}
  A product's illustration, or the dashed placeholder tile when it has none.

  The prototype drew these as CSS background-image on empty spans, which meant no
  srcset, no loading control and nothing for image search. These are real images
  off the product, so the grid renders store data.

  Height is set by the context that renders this (.pl-card__shot, .pl-stack, and
  so on), matching how the prototype sized them.

  Accepts: product, class, sizes, loading, fetchpriority, widths, prefer_hero

  prefer_hero swaps in the taller, narrower bottle the prototype's hero stage
  uses. Same product, different artwork: at a 680px stage the card art is 434px
  wide against the hero art's 220px, so three of them overrun the stage.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign media = product.featured_media

  if prefer_hero
    assign hero = product.metafields.purelane.hero_image.value
    if hero
      assign media = hero.image | default: hero
    endif
  endif

  assign img_loading = loading | default: 'lazy'
  assign img_widths = widths | default: '120,180,240,320,480,640'
  assign img_sizes = sizes | default: '160px'
  assign img_class = 'pl-pimg ' | append: class | strip
-%}
{%- if media -%}
  {{
    media
    | image_url: width: 640
    | image_tag:
      class: img_class,
      loading: img_loading,
      fetchpriority: fetchpriority,
      widths: img_widths,
      sizes: img_sizes,
      alt: media.alt | default: product.title | escape
  }}
{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Not an error state. The prototype already draws this tile for the fabric
    conditioner in the laundry combo, which has no illustration, so a product
    without media falls back to the design's own answer for it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <span class="pl-tile {{ class }}" role="img" aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }}">
    {% render 'purelane-icon', icon: 'leaf' %}
  </span>
{%- endif -%}
